wlcs v1.8.1: the xdg_popup tests' parent window attaches a buffer before the compositor's initial configure is acknowledged.

Same defect as 0001, in tests/xdg_popup.cpp: `XdgPopupStableManager` makes a toplevel and calls
`wait_for_frame_to_render()`, whose first commit carries a buffer. A compositor that enforces
xdg_surface.unconfigured_buffer closes the connection, so every `Anchor`, `Gravity`, `ConstraintAdjustment`
and `XdgPopupStable` test (about 70) failed before it tested a popup. The constructor now does the initial
commit and acknowledges the configure first.

Applied by scripts/wlcs.sh with `git apply`; drop it when wlcs fixes the fixture upstream.

diff --git a/tests/xdg_popup.cpp b/tests/xdg_popup.cpp
index e7582de..3e2aa6f 100644
--- a/tests/xdg_popup.cpp
+++ b/tests/xdg_popup.cpp
@@ -266,6 +266,24 @@ public:
           toplevel{std::in_place, xdg_shell_surface.value()},
           parent{&*xdg_shell_surface}
     {
+        // The initial commit carries no buffer; the compositor answers it with a configure, which has to be
+        // acknowledged before wait_for_frame_to_render() attaches one (xdg_surface.unconfigured_buffer).
+        bool initial_configure_received = false;
+        ON_CALL(xdg_shell_surface.value(), configure(testing::_))
+            .WillByDefault(
+                [&initial_configure_received, raw = static_cast<xdg_surface*>(xdg_shell_surface.value())](uint32_t serial)
+                {
+                    xdg_surface_ack_configure(raw, serial);
+                    initial_configure_received = true;
+                });
+        wl_surface_commit(surface);
+        client->dispatch_until([&initial_configure_received]() { return initial_configure_received; });
+        ON_CALL(xdg_shell_surface.value(), configure(testing::_))
+            .WillByDefault(
+                [raw = static_cast<xdg_surface*>(xdg_shell_surface.value())](uint32_t serial)
+                {
+                    xdg_surface_ack_configure(raw, serial);
+                });
         wait_for_frame_to_render();
     }
 
